(17) Such other provisions as the city reasonably determines are necessary or appropriate to permit the city to manage its streets or ensure compliance with the franchise or revocable license, to the extent not prohibited by law.
(b) The city manager shall make available to an applicant a model franchise or revocable license, as applicable, containing the terms and conditions the city seeks to impose pursuant to subsection (a). The city manager shall have the right to modify from time to time such model franchise or revocable license, so long as such modifications are consistent with this chapter and applicable law.
(Ord. No. 01-09, § 2.7, 9-10-2001)

1056:
(a) Bills to customers for city utility service shall be mailed out on such day or days of each month as may be determined as desirable by the city. Bills shall be paid at the city hall and a failure to receive bills or notices shall not prevent such bills from becoming delinquent nor relieve the consumer from payment of same. The failure of utility users or consumers to pay the charges duly imposed shall result in the automatic imposition of the following penalties:
(1) Nonpayment within ten (10) days from the due date shall subject the consumer to a penalty of ten (10) percent of the total delinquent account;
(2) Nonpayment within twenty (20) days from the due date will result in the utilities being shut off and discontinued from the utility user's or consumer's property;
(3) Nonpayment for sixty (60) days after the original due date will allow the city, in addition to all other rights and remedies, to terminate any type of contractual agreement or relationship with the consumer or customer; and in such event, the utility user shall not be entitled to receive, nor shall the city be obligated to supply, any utilities to that customer or property thereafter.
(b) Service disconnected for nonpayment of bills will be restored only after bills are paid in full, including any penalty, such security deposit as may be required by the mayor and council is made and paid in full, and a service charge of twenty-five dollars ($25.00) for each utility connection is paid for each meter reconnected.
(Code 1975, § 40-38; Ord. No. 03-09, § 1, 7-14-2003)

1057:
(a) When water and sewer service is discontinued and all bills are paid, the security deposit shall be refunded to the consumer by the city.
(b) Upon discontinuance of service for nonpayment of bills, the security deposit will be applied by the city toward settlement of the account. Any balance will be refunded to the consumer; however, if the security deposit is insufficient to cover the bill, the city may proceed to collect the balance in the usual way provided by law for collection of debts.
(c) The city reserves a right to discontinue its service without notice for the following additional reasons:
(1) To prevent fraud or abuse;
(2) Consumer's willful disregard of the city's rules;
(3) Emergency repairs;
(4) Insufficiency of water supply due to circumstances beyond the city's control;
(5) Legal processes;
(6) Direction of public authorities;
(7) Strike, riot, fire, flood or unavoidable accident.
(Code 1975, § 40-39)
